# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER COMMIT: LUKS header backups
#
# A LUKS header contains the master key, wrapped by your passphrase. Committing
# one to a repository — especially a PUBLIC one — hands an attacker everything
# except the passphrase, permanently, in a history that cannot be reliably
# scrubbed. Anyone who later learns or brute-forces the passphrase can decrypt
# the disk offline.
#
# Header backups belong on OFFLINE EXTERNAL MEDIA. Never here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*luks-header*
*luks-backup*
*.header
*.img

# Keys and secrets
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
secrets*
*password*
*passphrase*

# Unredacted diagnostics — contain serial numbers, the Dell service tag,
# MAC addresses and filesystem UUIDs.
diagnostics/*-unredacted*
diagnostics/*.raw

# Editor / OS noise
*~
*.swp
*.tmp
.DS_Store
